---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

// Same verified Unsplash photo used on the homepage hero (see index.astro
// for the licensing note) -- reused here at a smaller size since the
// About page's whole argument is built around this exact statue.
const neptunePhoto = "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1743634427797-cda09d4bcca7?w=900&q=80";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Quantex"
  description="Why Quantex is built around Neptune, the Roman god of the sea, and what that has to do with a trading bot."
>
  <section class="qx-about-hero">
    <div class="qx-container qx-about-hero-inner">
      <div class="qx-about-hero-copy">
        <span class="qx-eyebrow">Philosophy</span>
        <h1>Built like a trident</h1>
        <p class="qx-lead">
          The Quantex mark is a trident. That wasn't an accident. Neptune,
          the Roman god of the sea, carries one, and the sea is the oldest
          metaphor there is for a market: it moves whether you're watching
          it or not, and it doesn't care whether you're ready.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="qx-about-hero-art">
        <img
          src={neptunePhoto}
          alt="Bronze statue of Neptune holding a trident against a blue sky, the Fountain of Neptune in Bologna"
          loading="eager"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="qx-section">
    <div class="qx-container qx-prose">
      <h2>The sea moves. So does the market.</h2>
      <p>
        Nobody tells the tide to slow down, and nobody tells a crypto
        market to either. Prices swing on volume, on news, on nothing at
        all. You can fight that, try to read every candle yourself and
        catch every reversal by hand, or you can build something that
        holds a position in the current and works it automatically, the
        way a fisherman doesn't out-swim the sea, he learns its pattern
        and works with it.
      </p>
      <p>
        That's the whole idea behind Quantex. Deposit crypto, trade the
        spot market yourself when you want to, and hand the rest to a bot
        built to hold a position in the current without needing you to
        watch every wave.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="qx-section qx-section-alt">
    <div class="qx-container qx-prose">
      <h2>Three prongs, three strategies</h2>
      <p>
        Neptune's trident has three prongs. Quantex ships three bot
        strategies. That's the whole reason the mark looks the way it
        does.
      </p>
      <div class="qx-trident-grid">
        <div class="qx-trident-item">
          <h3>Grid</h3>
          <p>Works a range, buying low and selling high inside it, over and over, without needing to guess a direction.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="qx-trident-item">
          <h3>DCA</h3>
          <p>Buys on a schedule no matter what the price is doing, so no single bad entry decides the outcome.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="qx-trident-item">
          <h3>Momentum</h3>
          <p>Follows a trend once it actually forms, and steps aside the moment it stalls.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p>
        Spot trading is the fourth option: no bot at all, just you and the
        order book, for when you'd rather hold the trident yourself.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="qx-cta">
    <div class="qx-container qx-cta-inner">
      <div>
        <h2>Ready to trade?</h2>
        <p>Create an account, deposit crypto, and pick a strategy, including your own.</p>
        <a class="qx-btn-primary qx-btn-lg" href="https://trading.onquantex.com/signup">Trade Now</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .qx-about-hero {
    padding: var(--space-48) 0;
  }
  .qx-about-hero-inner {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-32);
  }
  .qx-about-hero-copy {
    flex: 1 1 480px;
  }
  .qx-about-hero-art {
    flex: 1 1 320px;
  }
  .qx-about-hero-art img {
    width: 100%;
    border-radius: var(--radius-2xl);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
  }
  .qx-eyebrow {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--font-data);
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--teal-base);
    background: var(--teal-pale);
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-8);
    border-radius: var(--radius-full);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-16);
  }
  .qx-about-hero-copy h1 {
    font-size: clamp(32px, 4.5vw, 48px);
    color: var(--ink-base);
  }
  .qx-lead {
    margin-top: var(--space-16);
    font-size: 18px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    max-width: 50ch;
  }

  .qx-section {
    padding: var(--space-48) 0;
  }
  .qx-section-alt {
    background: var(--cream-deep);
  }
  /* .qx-prose itself (max-width, h2/p sizing) lives in global.css now —
     shared with the blog, which renders raw markdown output that has no
     custom classes of its own to hook a page-scoped style onto. */

  .qx-trident-grid {
    margin: var(--space-24) 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-16);
  }
  .qx-trident-item {
    background: var(--cream-base);
    border: 1px solid var(--cream-line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-xl);
    padding: var(--space-20);
  }
  .qx-trident-item h3 {
    font-size: 17px;
    color: var(--teal-base);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }
  .qx-trident-item p {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .qx-cta {
    padding: var(--space-48) 0 var(--space-32);
  }
  .qx-cta-inner {
    background: var(--teal-deep);
    border-radius: var(--radius-2xl);
    padding: var(--space-48);
    text-align: center;
  }
  .qx-cta-inner h2 {
    color: var(--on-accent);
  }
  .qx-cta-inner p {
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
    color: var(--teal-sage);
    max-width: 48ch;
    margin-left: auto;
    margin-right: auto;
  }
  .qx-cta-inner .qx-btn-primary {
    margin-top: var(--space-16);
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .qx-about-hero-inner {
      flex-direction: column;
    }
    .qx-trident-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .qx-container {
      padding: 0 var(--space-16);
    }
    .qx-section {
      padding: var(--space-32) 0;
    }
    .qx-cta-inner {
      padding: var(--space-32) var(--space-24);
    }
  }
</style>
